claimed: intent-symbolic-tier — the tier the trigger never fired for, built anyway on the operator word, and measured as a hypothesis rather than shipped as a default. An LU dictionary is BM25 over labelled examples: okay-rag Postings is already a Fold and a Monoid, and Keyword.search already scores, so the tier is a projection of what exists, not new infrastructure. Honest split or it measures nothing: build the index from HALF the fixture and score the other half, never both. Three numbers decide it -- coverage (what fraction it answers at a given margin), agreement with gold on what it answers, and latency against the model tier. Linagora answer in under 150ms with no model at all, so the question is not whether a symbolic pass can work but whether ours pays here.
